## How to Fix It (The Solution)

  ## To break a deadlock using synchronized, you must enforce a strict, global lock ordering. We can use the object's unique system memory identity (System.identityHashCode) to
    #  ensure that regardless of the parameters passed, the locks are always acquired in the exact same sequence.

public static void safeTransfer(Account from, Account to, int amount) {
    int fromHash = System.identityHashCode(from);
    int toHash = System.identityHashCode(to);

    // Establish deterministic order
    Object firstLock = fromHash < toHash ? from : to;
    Object secondLock = fromHash < toHash ? to : from;

    synchronized (firstLock) {
        synchronized (secondLock) {
            from.balance -= amount;
            to.balance += amount;
            System.out.println(Thread.currentThread().getName() + " completed transfer safely.");
        }
    }
}
